          "thinking": "The user is asking a pricing/positioning question about two portfolio projects: acompose and umbra. This is a Portfolio Director role question. I need to load my role skill and personality skills, and the guardrail. Also there are relevant lore skills: lore-project-index (contains acompose and umbra), lore-self-compensation, lore-self-career-index (rate conversation, productized service, is this a business), lore-rule-disclosure-gradient.\n\nLet me first understand what acompose and umbra are. From the lore trigger list, umbra and acompose appear in lore-project-index. Let me load relevant skills.\n\nThe guardrail requires: strongest case against first, named reversal condition, verdict from a separate decision model (Jev). The decisive personality wants closed option set with recommendation first. Outward wants web search to validate market claims.\n\nLet me load the doctrine skills first. The role instructions say to load role-prod-director, boundaries, personalities, guardrail before acting.\n\nLet me also load lore-project-index and lore-self-compensation / lore-self-career-index for the rate conversation context.\n\nLet me do this efficiently. I'll load the skills in parallel.\n\nActually, let me think about what I actually need:\n1. role-prod-director (required)\n2. boundary-build-foundational-software\n3. boundary-modify-live-backend\n4. boundary-suggest-external-comms\n5. boundary-seek-external-validation\n6. personality-decisive\n7. personality-outward\n8. guardrail-unsycophantic-critique\n9. lore-project-index (to know what acompose and umbra are)\n10. lore-self-compensation (rate rules — standing rule against inventing comp preferences)\n11. lore-self-career-index (rate conversation, productized service, is this a business)\n\nThe key tension: lore-self-compensation has a \"standing rule against inventing comp preferences.\" So I must be careful — the question is about what someone might pay for a custom one-time cut + support, which is Kai's comp. I need to load lore-self-compensation to know what's confirmed vs inferred.\n\nAlso lore-rule-disclosure-gradient for what can be said publicly (this is about Kai's own projects and pricing, which is outward-facing potentially).\n\nLet me load these skills. I'll do them in a batch.",
