            "value": {
              "resultType": "complete",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "# Loaded Skill: lore-self-compensation (skill)\n\nThe single authoritative source for Kai's compensation rules, separating what she confirmed from what agents inferred, with a standing rule against inventing comp preferences. Triggers - comp, compensation, salary, base, floor, band, range, equity, negotiation, offer, what number, comp expectations, $250K, 250k, $200K, top of band, target number, stating a number, adding a number, recruiter reply, recruiter outreach, intro call, cover note, LinkedIn post about work, bio, what Kai is looking for, why Kai is looking, pitch, drafting anything outward about a role.\n\n## Content\n\n# compensation\n\nEvery role reads this before stating, assuming or drafting anything about Kai's compensation, Developer Advocate included: comp claims reach recruiters through drafted text more often than through a decision.\n\n## Do not invent comp preferences\n\n**Why this entry exists.** Kai flagged 2026-08-17 that agents keep filling in compensation preferences she does not hold.\n\n* If a rule is not in the confirmed section below, **do not state it, assume it, or draft from it.** Ask.\n* Do not derive a target from a market rate, a level, a title, a peer comp, or a published band. Those inform what a role pays, never what Kai wants.\n* Do not build negotiation prep, anchors, walk-away numbers, or \"what are you targeting\" answers unless Kai asks for them.\n* An older record is not confirmation. The audit closed 2026-08-17, so anything not confirmed below is not hers.\n\n## Confirmed\n\n**The floor is a sector split.** $170K nonprofit and government, $200K otherwise. $250K is the top anchor. Kai chose this 2026-08-17 from the recorded options, superseding the flat $170K floor and the $220K to $250K strongest-range framing.\n\n**Five days per week onsite is a hard stop.** Confirmed the same day. Not a compensation lever and not tradeable against a top-of-range offer.\n\n**Comp is not load-bearing.** Kai does not optimize for comp. No pre-drafted negotiation prep, no framing role-fit around a number, and comp questions come after role form, team, scope and lifestyle. Confirmed 2026-08-17.\n\n**The anchor is real.** Median offer $200K base, current and previous comp also $200K, $250K as median plus one standard deviation. Confirmed 2026-08-17. Above $250K is reach territory needing offer-stage leverage.\n\n**The rule rate is $150 an hour.** Stated 2026-08-24 and directed onto the public site, with 70% utilisation chosen alongside. Her first ever confirmed rule rate, so nothing earlier supersedes it. It is a rate rather than a floor, and no walk-away, premium tier or negotiation ladder is confirmed.\n\n**A rate and a salary floor are different units and do not compare.** Kai rejected that framing 2026-08-25. Do not derive an annual equivalent, do not set one against the FTE floor, and do not treat publishing both as a conflict.\n\n**Equity is not load-bearing.** Cap-table mechanics, 409A, exercise windows, refresh grants and vesting cliffs are out of scope. Confirmed 2026-08-17.\n\n## Rejected, do not reintroduce\n\n**\"The floor is a gate, not an ask, never presented to a recruiter as a target.\"** Kai declined this 2026-08-17. It claimed the recruiting board rather than her as its source, which marked it for audit. The board's scoring weight, comp at 8 of 120 points, is a board mechanic and stays on the board card. The normative guidance about how Kai presents her floor was never hers, so do not re-derive it from that weighting.\n\n## Placement\n\nSalary history lives here because the operational copy sits in a treat-as-public-safe repo. The hiring page matches Confirmed exactly. **The rule rate is not on the site**, `teable:coilyco-bridge/website#7062`, open pending Kai's ruling. Detail: [`references/placement.md`](references/placement.md).\nRelated: `lore-self-career-positioning`, `lore-self-career-direction`, and `lore-self-capacity-and-tenure` for the same anti-invention discipline on tenure drivers.\n\n## Supporting Files\n\nSkill directory: /private/var/folders/gt/p630435j2y3dmk7f_twxqqr40000gp/T/aos/native/zq56/evalrun/rh-new-3/.agents/skills/lore-self-compensation\n\nRelative paths in this skill resolve from the skill directory. The shell tool runs in the session working directory, so use the resolved path below or `cd` into the skill directory before running supporting scripts.\n\n- references/placement.md → /private/var/folders/gt/p630435j2y3dmk7f_twxqqr40000gp/T/aos/native/zq56/evalrun/rh-new-3/.agents/skills/lore-self-compensation/references/placement.md (load_skill(name: \"lore-self-compensation/references/placement.md\"))\n"
                }
              ],
              "isError": false
            }
          }
        }
      ],
