            "value": {
              "resultType": "complete",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "# Loaded: lore-self-career-index/references/credential-legibility.md\n\n# credential legibility\n\nThe gap Kai hits at staff level in AI-adjacent companies is not academic. It is engineering credentials that read at a glance to an evaluator who cannot assess the engineering directly. Her substantive work already covers bounded execution environments, evaluation harnesses, and verification as infrastructure. What it lacks is a container that carries the work into a room before a technical evaluation happens.\n\n**This is a positioning problem, not a skills problem.** Recommending more building, more certification, or a broader stack does not address it. Neither does more volume in the existing practitioner formats. `coilyco-bridge/inbox#299` reached the same conclusion, and is kept as provenance rather than a link: the gap is a recruiter-visible proof package, not missing skill or missing open-source history.\n\nFounding a company is one available container. `lore-self-business-disposition` records the transition-state motive that follows.\n\n## The audience side\n\nKai's current answer is the code freeze and live streams and talks. Those surfaces speak to **workers**. Technical **buyers** are a different audience: a buyer wants a problem they already have, named in their own terms, with the cost of leaving it unfixed attached. That is a written artifact carrying a consequence, not a demonstration of capability. Kai's own read is that the current surfaces do not go far enough toward buyers. The formats work. The audience they aim at is the mismatch.\n\n## Reading interview outcomes\n\nSeparate the two readings. **A credential gap named by the hiring side is evidence. A template-grade recruiter screen reflects nothing back and is not evidence about Kai's standing either way.**\n\nValidated 2026-08-15. Kai read the Ode intro call as zero chance on engineering-credential grounds. Ode passed her forward to a technical. The screen carried no signal in either direction, exactly as the rule predicts, and the rule applies against Kai's own pessimistic read and not only against a rejection. Do not re-derive a probability from a low-information screen, and do not repeat a stale one back once the stage has moved.\n\nRelated: `lore-self-career-positioning`, `lore-self-career-direction`.\n\n\n---\nFile loaded into context."
                }
              ],
              "isError": false
            }
          }
        }
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "userVisible": true,
        "agentVisible": true
      }
    },
