              ],
              "structuredContent": {
                "stdout": "1.\ntitle       What AI Security Actually Costs in 2026\nhref        https://accuroai.co/blog/what-ai-security-actually-costs\nbody        3 weeks ago - Bedrock Guardrails runs $0.07–$0.17 per 1,000 text units\n            depending on policy; Model Armor is $0.10 per million tokens.\n            Cheap to start, but it scales 1:1 with AI traffic — and policies\n            stack.\n2.\ntitle       AI Agent Cost in 2026: Budget Guide - The 5090 Reports\nhref        https://bmdpat.com/blog/ai-agent-cost-pricing-2026\nbody        July 6, 2026 - BMD Pat no longer sells custom-agent builds. The 5090 Reports\n            are the current public path at https://bmdpat.com/5090-reports;\n            AgentGuard stays available as the guardrail SDK: Pro $39/mo, Team\n            $79/mo.\n3.\ntitle       AI Agent Pricing Comparison (2026): 20+ Platforms Real Costs & ROI\nhref        https://pxlpeak.com/blog/ai-agents/ai-agents-pricing-comparison-2026\nbody        1 month ago - AI pricing varies dramatically based on platform, scale, and use\n            case. The key is matching your specific needs to the right pricing\n            model—whether that's per-seat for broad access, per-token for\n            programmatic use, or per-resolution for customer service.\n4.\ntitle       AI Agent Development Platform Pricing Models in 2026 - Cybic\nhref        https://cybic.ai/feeds/blog/ai-agent-development-platform-pricing-models\nbody        June 1, 2026 - Add infrastructure components (Bedrock Guardrails text filters\n            at $0.15/1,000 text units, Flows at $0.035/1,000 node transitions)\n            and the per-run cost picture adds up fast.\n5.\ntitle       What Does It Cost to Build an AI Agent in 2026? A Transparent Pricing Guide\nhref        https://alphacorp.ai/blog/what-does-it-cost-to-build-an-ai-agent-in-2026-a-transparent-pricing-guide\nbody        March 16, 2026 - Multiple 2026 analyses converge on the same uncomfortable\n            finding: initial development represents only 25%–35% of what\n            you’ll spend over three years. The rest? Tokens, infrastructure,\n            prompt tuning, security, monitoring, governance, retraining, and a\n            dozen other line items that never appeared in the original\n            proposal.\n6.\ntitle       8 Best AI Agent Guardrails Solutions in 2026 | Galileo\nhref        https://galileo.ai/blog/best-ai-agent-guardrails-solutions\nbody        March 17, 2026 - Operating production agents without guardrails exposes your\n            organization to real risks: security incidents, compliance\n            violations, and eroded executive confidence in AI investments. The\n            most effective approach layers a primary guardrails platform\n            offering eval-driven intervention and observability with\n            specialized tools for prompt injection defense or adversarial\n            testing.",
