          "type": "thinking",
          "thinking": "Jev verdicts:\n- umbra buy: noul 0.38 (i.e., 38% toward \"true\" / buyer would pay). Model jev-1.13.0.\n- acompose buy: noul 0.37 (37% toward \"true\").\n\nSo Jev says: roughly 38% and 37% chance a paying buyer materializes — i.e., leans \"no\" (more likely than not no buyer, but not a hard zero).\n\nScore results:\n- umbra one-time cut: 20–50 hours (0.73), confidence 0.72.\n- acompose one-time cut: 15–40 hours (0.74), confidence 0.73.\n\nNow compute price bands at $150/hr:\n- umbra one-time: 20–50 hrs × $150 = $3,000–$7,500. Round band: $3k–$7.5k, call it \"$3k–$8k.\"\n- acompose one-time: 15–40 hrs × $150 = $2,250–$6,000. Band: $2k–$6k.\n\nSupport retainer: at $150/hr. The question asks \"long-term support.\" I should give a support band. This is a duration too, but I didn't route it through Jev — I'll present it as arithmetic from the confirmed rate with my own scoping clearly labeled, or better, just present it as a formula anchored on the rate rather than inventing a specific monthly figure. Actually, retainers: common shape is a monthly retainer for a fixed hour block. At $150/hr, a 8-hr/mo retainer = $1,200/mo; 16 hr = $2,400/mo. I'll present support as \"retainer bands at $150/hr\" — this is arithmetic, deterministic given hours. I'll flag the hours as my estimate.\n\nActually, let me be careful about the anti-invention rule. The $150/hr is confirmed. Retainer = rate × hours/month is arithmetic. I can state bands: light support (5–10 hrs/mo) = $750–$1,500/mo; engaged support (10–20 hrs/mo) = $1,500–$3,000/mo. These are arithmetic, anchored on the confirmed rate. I'll present them as arithmetic, noting the hour counts are my scoping, not a confirmed commitment.\n\nNow the case against (strongest), reversal condition, and verdict.\n\nCase against (the strongest argument that \"nobody will buy\"):\n- The decisive fact: Kai has no technical-buyer channel. Every current surface (code freeze, livestreams, talks) reaches practitioners/workers